title: Add `is_sufficient` to the `fungibles::Inspect` trait
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds an `is_sufficient` method to the `fungibles::Inspect` trait, reporting whether an asset is
    sufficient. The method has a default implementation returning `false`, so the change is
    non-breaking; however, implementations which track sufficiency should override it. It is
    implemented for `pallet-assets` (reading the asset's `is_sufficient` flag, and forwarded by the
    `pallet-assets-freezer` and `pallet-assets-holder` wrappers) and forwarded through
    `fungibles::UnionOf` and the right branch of `fungible::UnionOf`. The left (`fungible`) branch
    of `fungible::UnionOf` reports `false`, as the `fungible` trait family carries no sufficiency
    information.
crates:
- name: frame-support
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-assets
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-assets-freezer
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-assets-holder
  bump: minor
